    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d956">

                <pb facs="0844" n="835" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg835"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.48/782: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-11-17T23:00:00+01:00">November 17,
                            1940—11 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 18—7:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>654. The Naval Attaché<anchor n="40" xml:id="d956-f1"/> informs me that he has
                    just been told by the chief of the Spanish Merchant Marine Shipping Board that
                    he has been ordered by the Minister of Industry and Commerce to hold in
                    readiness one-half of his tramp tonnage or approximately 350,000 tons of
                    shipping to be sent to a destination to be indicated later for the purpose of
                    bringing wheat to Spain of a total tonnage of 450 tons which will be supplied by
                    Germany.</p>
                <p>The British Chargé d’Affaires tells me that he has been informed that such an
                    offer has been made. However, I share the Naval Attaché’s entire skepticism as
                    to the feasibility of effective deliveries.</p>
                <p>The subject appears to be of interest as indicating the efforts which Germany is
                    now making to offset any offers of foodstuffs which might be made to Spain by
                    any other Governments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d956-f1" n="40" xml:id="d956-f1-content">
